  "id": "DrugBank_DB09260 - MONDO_5279",
  "verbalization": "Parnaparin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Pulmonary Embolism (PE) through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Parnaparin may be associated with Purpura Fulminans, a severe form of purpura, which in turn is linked to Heparin, Bovine, and ultimately to PE. This pathway implies that Parnaparin could potentially exert a role in the development of PE, possibly through mechanisms involving anticoagulant or anti-inflammatory effects. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Parnaparin to PE, with consistent scores across different paths, supports the hypothesis that Parnaparin may have a role in the pathophysiology of PE, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, but further research is needed to confirm the specific biological pathways involved.",
